SLIDE 03 | 0:45 | One provider can create 1,000+ interpretation paths
DELIVERY: Tell this as a human investigation, moving left to right.

Mercy General illustrates the real problem: 109 files, four base agreements, 66 sub-contract IDs, and parallel contract chains. An analyst cannot simply search for a rate. They must identify plausible files, reconstruct the amendment history, separate parallel versions, and often ask a contract expert which document was executed. That creates more than a thousand possible interpretation paths. The danger is not only lost time. A stale but plausible answer can apply a superseded reimbursement term, miss a renewal window, or leave an audit trail that has to be rebuilt manually.

