SLIDE 07 | 0:35 | Four retrieval channels recover complete evidence
DELIVERY: Contrast the four channels; avoid deep algorithm detail.

Generic RAG normally embeds text and retrieves the nearest passages. CIP uses four channels because legal and financial questions fail in different ways. Semantic search handles varied language. Lexical search finds exact terms and dollar values. Metadata and SQL apply provider, date, and current-state filters. Structural retrieval follows related clauses and amendment chains. Reciprocal-rank fusion combines that evidence, and domain normalization maps inconsistent labels to a common taxonomy. This is contract reasoning, not simple document search.

TRANSITION: The application then turns this governed evidence into a usable business experience.

