SLIDE 09 | 0:50 | Trust and cost are engineered together
DELIVERY: Stress that most controls are deterministic and zero-token.

Before a question is answered, five pipeline gates have already checked OCR quality, extraction structure, data integrity, contract state, and retrieval readiness. After the question, layered controls validate routing, numeric consistency, provider identity, dates, absence claims, grounding, citations, and completeness. If evidence is insufficient, the system should refuse or lower confidence rather than manufacture certainty. Most of these checks use Python, SQL, and rules - not another LLM call. The same philosophy controls cost: simple work stays deterministic, tools retrieve only what is needed, and current testing keeps even complicated answers typically below one dollar of LLM inference, excluding shared Databricks compute.

